━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ StateMachines is facet of Checker
    sees Loops
    sees Streams

_ machine-handed = false

────────────────────
+ do check-machine-site TypeId
    - id SyntaxId

` A state machine where it is written: its own function, typed once, is called there to start
` it, recorded at the machine, and answers the value it starts in, of the machine's union. The
` errors that leave its start leave the function there (see `check-machine`). A machine the
` binder bound no function for has no shape here.
. decl = nested-decl-of(id)
if decl == 0
    decline(id)
    = invalid-type
. callee = demand-nested(decl, no-type)
do facts.record-call(instance, id, callee, .call-function, scratch.no-fills, false)
note-unit-errors(callee, id)
. machine = facts.machine-of(callee)
= if machine then facts.root-machine(machine).union else invalid-type

────────────────────
+ do check-machine
    - id SyntaxId

` The function of a state machine, typed as one body though the emitter makes several functions
` of it: the one that starts it, and for each group of event transitions the one its
` subscriber runs. Its shape is checked first (`machine-shape`), then each part is typed once,
` in an order where what it reads is known (`type-machine`). It answers its union where it
` starts. One that refines the machine of a property of its class's base answers nothing: that
` machine starts after it, and keeps the value (`inherited-machine`).
prepare()
. items = tree.state-items(tree.state-body(id))
. row = bindings.machine-slots(module, id)
. store = machine-placement(id, row) if row
. union = no-type
machine-handed = false
machining = machining.outer-starts = true
machining = machining.refined = no-instance
. refined = inherited-machine(id, items, store) if row && store
if !row || !store
    decline(id)
else if refined && machine-shape(id, items, store)
    machining = machining.refined = refined
    union = type-machine(id, items, row, store)
. answered = if union != no-type && machining.refined == no-instance then union else types.void-type
instances.set-returns(instance, answered, answered, .return-declared)
finish-errors(frame)
close()

────────────────────
_ do inherited-machine InstanceId?
    - id SyntaxId
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - store MachineStore

` The machine a property's machine refines, as the reference merges them: that of the property
` of the same name of the base of the class, through the instance that types the base's value
` for the class that declares it, as the class the machine is typed for holds it, which every
` class below shares, where the base has one; no instance where it has none, or the machine
` is no property's. A
` property of that name that holds no machine is the reference's error, as is a refinement that
` changes what the reference forbids (`refines-shaped`). One a class's markup writes refines that
` of the markup of a class above (`inherited-content-machine`).
if store == .store-content
    = inherited-content-machine(id, items)
if store != .store-member
    = no-instance
. property = machine-property(id)
. decls = program.modules[module].decls
. name Atom? = null
. owner-decl DeclId = 0
. site = id
do match? decls[property]
    | .decl-property(found)
        name = found.name
        owner-decl = found.owner
        site = found.syntax
if !name || owner-decl == 0
    = no-instance
. mark = scratch.types.mark
. owner = types.class-pattern-with-args(module, owner-decl, mark)
if owner == invalid-type
    = no-instance
types.complete(owner)
. base = types.base-of(owner) ?? no-type
. place = property-named(base, name) if base != no-type
if !place
    = no-instance
. level = types.properties[place].owner
. ref = class-ref(types, level)
. inherited = class-property(ref, name)
. value = declared-value(ref.module, inherited)
. machine = program.modules[ref.module].tree.declared-machine(value)
if machine == 0
    . message = "Inherited property '${name.text}' is not a state machine"
    frame.diagnose(site, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
    = null
. enclosing = instances.rows[instance].enclosing
. receiver = if enclosing != no-instance then holding-type(enclosing-self, ref) else level
    .. enclosing-self = instances.rows[enclosing].self-type
. unit = instances.intern-initializer(ref.module, inherited, receiver)
if instances.rows[unit].state == .instance-in-progress
    decline(id)
    = null
demand-own-body(unit)
for found in facts.machines
    . same = found.module == ref.module && found.syntax == machine && found.outer == 0
    if same && instances.rows[found.instance].enclosing == unit
        . names [Atom]
        . parents [U32]
        inherited-cases(found, names, parents)
        if !refines-shaped(items, U32.max, names, parents)
            = null
        = found.instance
decline(id)
= null

────────────────────
_ do inherited-content-machine InstanceId?
    - id SyntaxId
    - items [SyntaxId]

` The machine a machine written as a line of a class's markup refines, as a property's machine
` refines its base's: the first machine of the markup of a class above, from the nearest up,
` that has a case at its root of a name one of this machine's cases at its root has, through
` the function that fills the object with that class's markup, which the function this machine
` is written in runs; no instance where none has. A refinement that changes what the reference
` forbids is its error (`refines-shaped`).
. roots [Atom]
for item in items
    if tree.nodes[item] is .node-state-case
        roots += tree.state-name(item)!
. fill = instances.rows[instance].enclosing
while fill != no-instance
    . call = facts.filler-of(fill)
    if call == no-fact
        = no-instance
    fill = facts.calls[call].callee
    . level = instances.rows[fill].self-type
    if level == no-type || level == invalid-type
        = no-instance
    . ref = class-ref(types, level)
    . owner = program.modules[ref.module].tree
    . content SyntaxId = 0
    do match? program.modules[ref.module].decls[ref.decl]
        | .decl-class(class)
            content = class.content
    for machine in owner.content-machines(content)
        if names-root(owner, machine, roots)
            if instances.rows[fill].state == .instance-in-progress
                decline(id)
                = null
            demand-own-body(fill)
            for found in facts.machines
                . same = found.module == ref.module && found.syntax == machine && found.outer == 0
                if same && instances.rows[found.instance].enclosing == fill
                    . names [Atom]
                    . parents [U32]
                    inherited-cases(found, names, parents)
                    if !refines-shaped(items, U32.max, names, parents)
                        = null
                    = found.instance
            decline(id)
            = null
= no-instance

────────────────────
_ do names-root Bool
    - owner AST
    - machine SyntaxId
    - roots [Atom]

` Whether a machine has a case at its root of one of some names.
for item in owner.state-items(owner.state-body(machine))
    if owner.nodes[item] is .node-state-case && roots.find(owner.state-name(item)!) != null
        = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do inherited-cases
    - machine MachineFact
    - names [Atom]
    - parents [U32]

` The cases a machine has, each with the place of the case it is written in, or none at the
` root: those written in it, and where it refines another machine, those of that machine with
` the ones it adds.
. owner = program.modules[machine.module].tree
. items = owner.state-items(owner.state-body(machine.syntax))
if machine.refined == no-instance
    written-cases(owner, items, U32.max, names, parents)
    =
. above = facts.machine-of(machine.refined)
if !above
    =
inherited-cases(above, names, parents)
added-cases(owner, items, U32.max, names, parents)

────────────────────
_ do written-cases
    - owner AST
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - parent U32
    - names [Atom]
    - parents [U32]

` Each case written in a body and in theirs, under the case at a place.
for item in items
    if owner.nodes[item] is .node-state-case
        . place = names.length as U32
        names += owner.state-name(item)!
        parents += parent
        written-cases(owner, owner.state-items(owner.state-body(item)), place, names, parents)

────────────────────
_ do added-cases
    - owner AST
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - parent U32
    - names [Atom]
    - parents [U32]

` The cases a refinement's body adds under the case at a place: one it names again is refined,
` and adds those of its own body; any other is added with each case written in it.
for item in items
    if owner.nodes[item] is .node-state-case
        . found = case-under(owner.state-name(item)!, parent, names, parents)
        if found != U32.max
            added-cases(owner, owner.state-items(owner.state-body(item)), found, names, parents)
        else
            . place = names.length as U32
            names += owner.state-name(item)!
            parents += parent
            written-cases(owner, owner.state-items(owner.state-body(item)), place, names, parents)

────────────────────
_ do case-under U32
    - name Atom
    - parent U32
    - names [Atom]
    - parents [U32]

` The place of the case of a name written under the case at a place, or none.
for place in 0 .. < names.length
    if names[place] == name && parents[place] == parent
        = place as U32
= U32.max

────────────────────
_ do refines-shaped Bool
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - parent U32
    - names [Atom]
    - parents [U32]

` Whether a refinement's body changes only what the reference lets it, under the case of the
` inherited machine at a place: each case it names again keeps that case's trigger and what it
` holds, and each case it adds is written under a case, with a name the inherited machine does
` not use. Anything but a case written at the root has no shape here yet.
for item in items
    if !(tree.nodes[item] is .node-state-case)
        if parent == U32.max
            decline(item)
            = false
        continue
    . name = tree.state-name(item)!
    . found = case-under(name, parent, names, parents)
    if found == U32.max
        if names.find(name) != null
            . message = "State case '${name.text}' is declared elsewhere in the inherited machine"
            frame.diagnose(item, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
            = false
        if parent == U32.max
            . message = "Refinement cannot add top-level state case '${name.text}'"
            frame.diagnose(item, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
            = false
        continue
    if tree.state-targets(item).count != 0 || tree.state-trigger(item) != 0
        . message = "Refined state case '${name.text}' cannot change its trigger or payload"
        frame.diagnose(item, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
        = false
    if !refines-shaped(tree.state-items(tree.state-body(item)), found, names, parents)
        = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do machine-placement MachineStore?
    - id SyntaxId
    - row MachineSlots

` Where a machine keeps its value: in the local or the lazy local it is declared into, which
` starts it where it is first read, in the global of the module or the property of the class it
` is the value of, in the flags of the object whose markup it is a line of, or nowhere, written
` as a statement of a function that is no markup of a class. One written in the markup of a
` class otherwise has no shape here yet.
if row.bound != no-slot
    . kind = bindings.slots[row.bound].kind
    = .store-local if kind == .slot-local || kind == .slot-lazy
. property = machine-property(id)
if property != 0
    do match? program.modules[module].decls[property]
        | .decl-property(found)
            = if found.owner == 0 then .store-global else .store-member
    = null
. owner = frame.outer
if owner && owner.declaration.is-content
    = .store-content if tree.content-machines(owner.declaration.syntax).find(id) != null
= .store-none

────────────────────
_ do machine-property DeclId
    - id SyntaxId

` The property of the module whose value a machine is, or none.
. decls = program.modules[module].decls
for position in 0 .. < decls.length
    do match? decls[position]
        | .decl-property(property)
            if property.value == id
                = position as DeclId
= 0

────────────────────
_ do machine-shape Bool
    - id SyntaxId
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - store MachineStore

` Whether a machine is one the reference builds: no case is written twice, each fallback
` follows a group of transitions, each handler is on one source with at most a `when`, no
` decision made on entry enters a case again (`entries-settle`), and one a local, a global or a
` property names starts in a case. Each is the reference's error. A
` fallback that names values, and a case of a machine of a class's markup whose name the class
` declares otherwise, have no shape here yet.
. redefined = tree.redefined-case(items)
if redefined != 0
    . name = tree.state-name(redefined)!
    frame.diagnose
        - redefined
        - .stated
        - program.store-atom("Redefinition of state case '${name.text}'")
    = false
. misplaced = tree.misplaced-fallback(items)
if misplaced != 0
    frame.diagnose(misplaced, .stated, program.store-atom("State fallback has no transition group"))
    = false
if !handlers-shaped(items) || !entries-settle(items)
    = false
if stored-machine && tree.initial-case(items) == 0 && items.length != 0
    frame.diagnose(items[0], .stated, program.store-atom("State machine has no initial state"))
    = false
.. stored-machine = store != .store-none && store != .store-content
if store == .store-content
    for node in tree.machine-cases(items)
        if !flagged(node)
            . name = tree.state-name(node)
            . shown = if name then name.text else ""
            . message = "A case of a machine in a class's markup is read as a property of its name, and the class declares \"$shown\" already; rename the case or the property"
            frame.diagnose(node, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
            = false
. unbuilt = unbuilt-part(items)
if unbuilt != 0
    decline(unbuilt)
    = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do entries-settle Bool
    - items [SyntaxId]

` Whether the decisions made where a machine's cases are entered, with no trigger, never enter a
` case again, as the reference checks them from its first case and from each case written in
` it. Where one does, it is the reference's error at the decision.
. roots [SyntaxId]
. initial = tree.initial-case(items)
if initial != 0
    roots += initial
for node in tree.explicit-cases(items)
    roots += node
for root in roots
    . entering [SyntaxId]
    entering += root
    if !case-entries-settle(items, entering, root, 0)
        = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do case-entries-settle Bool
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - entering [SyntaxId]
    - node SyntaxId
    - decision SyntaxId

` Whether the decisions made where a case is entered, past the cases already `entering`, enter
` none of them again: each immediate transition of its body, up to one with no trigger, which
` always passes, and its first case, entered by the decision that led to the case.
. body = tree.state-items(tree.state-body(node))
for transition in tree.immediate-transitions(body)
    if !enter-decided(items, entering, tree.immediate-path(items, node, transition), transition)
        = false
    if tree.state-trigger(transition) == 0
        = true
. initial = tree.initial-case(body)
if initial == 0
    = true
. path [SyntaxId]
path += initial
= enter-decided(items, entering, path, decision)

────────────────────
_ do enter-decided Bool
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - entering [SyntaxId]
    - path [SyntaxId]
    - decision SyntaxId

` Whether entering the cases of a path by a decision enters none of the cases already
` `entering`, nor do the decisions made where its last case is entered.
. depth = entering.length
for node in path
    if entering.find(node) != null
        . name = tree.state-name(node)!
        . message = "Entry decisions loop back to '${name.text}' without a trigger"
        frame.diagnose
            - if decision != 0 then decision else node
            - .stated
            - program.store-atom(message)
        = false
    entering += node
. settled = case-entries-settle(items, entering, path[path.length - 1], decision)
while entering.length > depth
    entering.pop()
= settled

────────────────────
_ do handlers-shaped Bool
    - items [SyntaxId]

` Whether each handler of a machine's bodies is one the reference builds: on a single source,
` with no clause but one `when`. Each other is the reference's error.
for item in items
    if tree.is-transition(item) && !handlers-shaped(tree.state-items(tree.state-body(item)))
        = false
    if !tree.is-state-handler(item)
        continue
    do match? tree.nodes[item]
        | .node-for-block(row)
            do match? tree.nodes[row.loop]
                | .node-loop-syntax(loop)
                    if loop.next != 0 || row.next != 0
                        . message = "A state handler subscribes to a single source"
                        frame.diagnose(item, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
                        = false
                    do match? tree.nodes[loop.clause]
                        | .node-clause(clause)
                            if !(clause.op is .when-clause) || clause.next != 0
                                . message = "A state handler accepts only a when clause"
                                frame.diagnose(loop.clause, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
                                = false
= true

────────────────────
+ do flagged Bool
    - node SyntaxId

` Whether the class declares the flag of a case of a machine its markup writes, or its projection.
for decl in program.modules[module].decls
    do match? decl
        | .decl-property(row)
            if row.flag == node || row.projection == node
                = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do unbuilt-part SyntaxId
    - items [SyntaxId]

` The first part of a machine's bodies that has no shape here yet: a fallback that names values.
for item in items
    if tree.nodes[item] is .node-state-fallback && tree.state-targets(item).count != 0
        = item
    if tree.is-transition(item)
        . inner = unbuilt-part(tree.state-items(tree.state-body(item)))
        if inner != 0
            = inner
= 0

────────────────────
_ do type-machine TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - row MachineSlots
    - store MachineStore
    - outer SyntaxId = 0
    - parent SyntaxId = 0

` Types a machine's parts, the root first, then each case and continuation once what its
` activation sees is known (`activation-known`); one that never is has no shape here. What each
` activation sees is foreseen first where it can be (`foresee-activations`), so that the parts
` can read the machine by its name (`early-union`). Then the machine's union is made, of each
` case it names with what that case holds, and what it keeps is typed, and each projection of a
` machine written as a statement: a case's flag, or its payload where it is active. What each
` transition gives is converted to what its case holds, and the machine is recorded, with the
` machine around it and the case it is written in where it is a named machine written in a case
` of another.
machining = machining.store = store
machining = machining.syntax = id
machining = machining.items = items
machining = machining.cases = tree.machine-cases(items)
machining = machining.kept = tree.machine-captures(items, machining.cases)
machining.payloads.clear()
machining.kept-types.clear()
machining.starts.clear()
machining.typed.clear()
machining.waiting.clear()
machining.groups-found.clear()
for position in 0 .. < machining.cases.length
    machining.payloads += fixed-payload(position as U32)
    . unknown [TypeId]
    for _ in machining.kept[position]
        unknown += no-type
    machining.kept-types += unknown
do foresee-activations()
early-union(id, row, store)
note-starts(items)
type-machine-body(0, items)
. progress = true
while progress
    progress = false
    for position in 0 .. < machining.waiting.length
        . node = machining.waiting[position]
        if node != 0 && activation-known(node)
            machining.waiting[position] = 0
            type-machine-body(node, tree.state-items(tree.state-body(node)))
            progress = true
    if !progress
        progress = foresee-activations()
for node in machining.waiting
    if node != 0
        decline(node)
        = no-type
for payload in machining.payloads
    if payload == no-type || payload == invalid-type
        decline(id)
        = no-type
. union = machine-union(id, row)
type-machine-slots(row, union)
type-projections(id, store)
convert-targets()
. start = facts.machine-groups.length
for group in machining.groups-found
    facts.machine-groups.append(group)
. groups = RowRange'MachineGroup(start as U32, (facts.machine-groups.length - start) as U32)
. property = if store == .store-global || store == .store-member then machine-property(id) else 0
. fact = MachineFact
    - instance
    - id
    - union
    - store
    - module
    - property
    - groups
    - outer
    - parent
    - machining.refined
facts.machines.append(fact)
if (store == .store-member || store == .store-content) && outer == 0 && machining.refined == no-instance
    demand-machine-stops()
= union

────────────────────
_ do demand-task-owner

` The constructor of the `TaskOwner` a case makes as it is entered, where its activation owns
` the tasks spawned for it.
if facts.task-owner-make != no-instance || types.task-owner-type == invalid-type
    =
facts.task-owner-make = calls.demand-constructor(types.task-owner-type, scratch.types.mark)

────────────────────
_ do demand-machine-stops

` The event runtime's `event-own-machine`, which a machine a class's property holds or its markup
` writes gives what stops it as it starts, its `event-stop-machines`, which runs those of an
` object as the `close` of its class starts, and its `event-close-stopped`, which closes the
` object's events as that `close` leaves.
if facts.machine-stop != no-instance || types.event-endpoint-decl.module == 0
    =
. pointer = pointer-to(types.type-row(.uint8))
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(pointer)
. none = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(types.intern-function(types.void-type, false, none, none))
facts.machine-own = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - types.event-endpoint-decl.module
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("event-own-machine")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
scratch.types.push(pointer)
facts.machine-stop = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - types.event-endpoint-decl.module
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("event-stop-machines")
    - mark
facts.machine-close = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - types.event-endpoint-decl.module
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom("event-close-stopped")
    - mark
scratch.types.rewind(mark)

────────────────────
_ do early-union
    - id SyntaxId
    - row MachineSlots
    - store MachineStore

` Where what every case holds is fixed or foreseen before anything is typed, the machine's union
` is made first, so that its cases can read the machine by its name: the local or the lazy local
` it is kept in, the module's or the class's property it is, or the name a named machine written
` in a case of another declares. Elsewhere such a read waits for the union and has no shape here.
` A machine that refines another is read as the union of the machine none refines, made already.
if machining.refined != no-instance
    . above = facts.machine-of(machining.refined)
    if above
        facts.early-unions.append(EarlyUnion(instance, module, id, facts.root-machine(above).union))
    =
for payload in machining.payloads
    if payload == no-type
        =
. union = machine-union(id, row)
if row.bound != no-slot && store == .store-local && frame.outer
    frame.outer.assign(row.bound, union)
else if row.bound != no-slot && store == .store-nested
    frame.assign(row.bound, union)
else if store == .store-global || store == .store-member
    facts.early-unions.append(EarlyUnion(instance, module, id, union))

────────────────────
_ fixed-payload TypeId
    - position U32

` What a case holds where that is known before anything is typed: nothing where nothing names
` it with values; `U8` where the source of its payload gives none (`gives-nothing`), as the
` reference falls back to. Otherwise no type, until its source is typed (`settle-payload`), with
` or without a trigger.
|? !source
    types.void-type
|? gives-nothing(source)
    types.type-row(.uint8)
??
    no-type

.. source = tree.payload-source(machining.items, tree.state-name(machining.cases[position])!)

────────────────────
+ do gives-nothing Bool
    - source StateSource

` Whether a source of a case's payload gives no value, as the reference finds none there: a
` case one of whose names neither its trigger, if it has one, nor its owner's trigger captures.
if !(tree.nodes[source.node] is .node-state-case)
    = false
. trigger = tree.state-trigger(source.node)
. captures [Atom]
if trigger != 0
    tree.pattern-names(tree.trigger-pattern(trigger), captures)
if source.owner != 0
    tree.pattern-names(tree.trigger-pattern(tree.state-trigger(source.owner)), captures)
for target in tree.children[tree.state-targets(source.node)]
    do match? tree.nodes[target]
        | .node-identifier(named)
            if captures.find(named.name) == null
                = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do foresee-activations Bool

` Settles what the activation of each case sees before the machine's parts are typed, and
` again where no case or continuation waiting is known, as the reference infers it apart from
` where anything fires: what each case holds, from the source of its payload that nothing has
` typed, and each name it keeps, from each transition that enters it, each transition typed on
` trial (`foresee-in`), until nothing more settles. Whether anything is settled so.
. sources [SyntaxId]
. unsettled = false
for position in 0 .. < machining.cases.length
    . source SyntaxId = 0
    if machining.payloads[position] == no-type
        . found = tree.payload-source(machining.items, tree.state-name(machining.cases[position])!)
        if found && machining.typed.find(found.node) == null
            source = found.node
    sources += source
    if source != 0 || machining.kept-types[position].find(no-type) != null
        unsettled = true
if !unsettled
    = false
. settled = false
. chain [SyntaxId]
while foresee-in(machining.items, chain, sources)
    settled = true
= settled

────────────────────
_ do foresee-in Bool
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - chain [SyntaxId]
    - sources [SyntaxId]

` The transitions written among a body's items and in their bodies, each with the cases and
` continuations whose bodies it is written in, outermost first (`foresee-entry`). Whether
` anything is settled so.
. settled = false
for item in items
    if !tree.is-transition(item)
        continue
    if foresee-entry(item, items, chain, sources)
        settled = true
    chain += item
    if foresee-in(tree.state-items(tree.state-body(item)), chain, sources)
        settled = true
    chain.pop()
= settled

────────────────────
_ do foresee-entry Bool
    - transition SyntaxId
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - chain [SyntaxId]
    - sources [SyntaxId]

` A transition typed on trial where something of the case it enters is unsettled
` (`trial-transition`), with the names the activations around it see where they are known
` (`activation-names`): each name the case keeps that it reads there takes the type it has
` there, and what the case holds, where the transition is the source of its payload, is what it
` gives, or a tuple of them. Whether either is settled so.
. position = tree.case-position(machining.cases, tree.state-name(transition)!)
if position == null
    = false
. sourced = sources[position] == transition && machining.payloads[position] == no-type
. places [Size]
. wanted [SlotId]
if machining.kept-types[position].find(no-type) != null
    for read in bindings.machine-reads
        if read.module != module || read.site != transition || read.slot == no-slot
            continue
        . place = machining.kept[position].find(read.name)
        if place != null && machining.kept-types[position][place] == no-type
            places += place
            wanted += read.slot
if wanted.length == 0 && !sourced
    = false
. slots [SlotId]
. given [TypeId]
for part in chain
    activation-names(part, slots, given)
. found [TypeId]
. targets [TypeId]
trial-transition(transition, items, slots, given, wanted, found, targets)
. settled = false
if found.length == wanted.length
    for offset in 0 .. < wanted.length
        if found[offset] != no-type && found[offset] != invalid-type
            machining.kept-types[position][places[offset]] = found[offset]
            settled = true
if !sourced || targets.length == 0
    = settled
for target in targets
    if target == no-type || target == invalid-type
        = settled
settle-given(position, targets)
= true

────────────────────
_ do note-starts
    - items [SyntaxId]

` The cases and continuations a body enters as it is entered, and so as the machine starts:
` its first case and those its immediate transitions enter, and so on in each of theirs.
. initial = tree.initial-case(items)
if initial != 0
    note-start(initial)
for transition in tree.immediate-transitions(items)
    note-start(transition)

────────────────────
_ do note-start
    - node SyntaxId

if machining.starts.find(node) != null
    =
machining.starts += node
if tree.nodes[node] is .node-state-continuation
    . target = tree.find-case(machining.items, tree.state-name(node)!)
    if target != 0
        note-start(target)
        =
note-starts(tree.state-items(tree.state-body(node)))

────────────────────
_ do activation-known Bool
    - node SyntaxId

` Whether what the activation of a case or a continuation sees is known: what the case it
` enters holds and each name it keeps.
. position = tree.case-position(machining.cases, tree.state-name(node)!)
if position == null
    = true
if machining.payloads[position] == no-type
    = false
for type in machining.kept-types[position]
    if type == no-type
        = false
= true

────────────────────
_ do type-machine-body
    - owner SyntaxId
    - items [SyntaxId]

` One body of a machine: the root, a case or a continuation. The names its activation sees take
` their types (`bind-activation`), its entry statements are typed, then what runs once they
` have (`type-entered`), the functions of its groups (`type-handlers`), and its `do finally`
` blocks, each in a region of its own, which no narrowing leaves. Its cases and continuations
` wait their turn. What leaves a part only a handler runs is no error of the function
` (`hand-off-since`). A named machine among its entry statements is typed where it is written
` (`type-nested-machine`).
. starts = machining.outer-starts && (owner == 0 || machining.starts.find(owner) != null)
. mark = scratch.outgoing.mark
. narrowed = scratch.narrowings.mark
if owner != 0
    bind-activation(owner)
    for item in items
        if tree.nested-machine(item) != 0
            type-nested-machine(owner, item, starts)
        else if tree.is-entry-item(item)
            do check-statement(item)
type-entered(owner, items)
end-machine-region(narrowed)
hand-off-since(mark, starts)
. handlers = scratch.outgoing.mark
type-handlers(owner, items)
end-machine-region(narrowed)
hand-off-since(handlers, false)
. exits = scratch.outgoing.mark
if owner != 0
    for item in items
        if tree.nodes[item] is .node-do-finally-block
            do check-statement(item)
end-machine-region(narrowed)
hand-off-since(exits, starts)
for item in items
    if tree.is-transition(item)
        machining.waiting += item

────────────────────
_ do type-nested-machine
    - parent SyntaxId
    - item SyntaxId
    - starts Bool

` A named machine written in a case of the machine being typed, part of its function, as the
` reference builds it: typed as a machine is, while what is known of the machine around it is
` put aside, and recorded with that machine and the case. Its parts start with the machine
` around it where the case does. It is the reference's error that it has no first case.
. machine = tree.nested-machine(item)
. row = bindings.machine-slots(module, machine)
if !row
    decline(item)
    =
. own = machining
. fresh-payloads [TypeId]
. fresh-kept-types [[TypeId]]
. fresh-starts [SyntaxId]
. fresh-typed [SyntaxId]
. fresh-waiting [SyntaxId]
. fresh-found [MachineGroup]
machining = Machining
    - own.syntax
    - own.store
    - no-instance
    - tree.nested-machine-name(item)
    - starts
    - own.items
    - own.cases
    - own.kept
    - fresh-payloads
    - fresh-kept-types
    - fresh-starts
    - fresh-typed
    - fresh-waiting
    - fresh-found
. nested = tree.state-items(tree.state-body(machine))
if machine-shape(machine, nested, .store-nested)
    do type-machine(machine, nested, row, .store-nested, own.syntax, parent)
machining = own

────────────────────
_ do end-machine-region
    - mark ScratchMark

` Ends a part of a machine, which runs where others may not have: what the flow knew in it
` holds no longer.
frame.pop-narrowing(mark)
frame.doubt-members()

────────────────────
_ do hand-off-since
    - mark ScratchMark
    - starts Bool

` What leaves a part of a machine since a mark. A handler gives each error that leaves it to the
` global `unhandled-error` (see `hands-off`), typed once for the machine, as the reference's
` handlers do; the errors of a part only a handler runs then leave nothing, and those of a part
` that runs as the machine starts leave its function too. A call there whose callee's errors are
` not yet known lets them out all the same, to where the handler gives them.
if scratch.outgoing.mark == mark
    =
if !machine-handed
    machine-handed = true
    if !hands-off(instance)
        decline(frame.declaration.syntax)
if !starts
    for row in scratch.outgoing.since(mark)
        if row.call != U32.max
            facts.calls[row.call].propagates = true
    scratch.outgoing.rewind(mark)

────────────────────
_ do bind-activation
    - node SyntaxId

` The names a case's or a continuation's activation sees take their types
` (`activation-names`).
. slots [SlotId]
. given [TypeId]
activation-names(node, slots, given)
for offset in 0 .. < slots.length
    frame.assign(slots[offset], given[offset])

────────────────────
_ do activation-names
    - node SyntaxId
    - slots [SlotId]
    - given [TypeId]

` The names a case's or a continuation's activation sees, as the reference binds them, each
` added to `slots` with its type added to `given`: a name among what it gives takes the part of
` what the case holds in its place, where that is known, and a name the case keeps what it
` keeps.
. position = tree.case-position(machining.cases, tree.state-name(node)!)
if position == null
    =
. payload = machining.payloads[position]
. targets = tree.state-targets(node)
. offset = 0u32
for target in tree.children[targets]
    do match? tree.nodes[target]
        | .node-identifier(named)
            . slot = bindings.declared-at(frame.slots, node, named.name)
            . part = if whole-payload then payload else payload-part(payload, offset)
                .. whole-payload = targets.count == 1 || payload == no-type
            if slot != no-slot && part != no-type
                slots += slot
                given += part
    offset += 1
. kept = machining.kept[position]
. names [Atom]
tree.target-names(node, names)
for place in 0 .. < kept.length
    . slot = bindings.declared-at(frame.slots, node, kept[place])
    if slot != no-slot && names.find(kept[place]) == null
        slots += slot
        given += machining.kept-types[position][place]

────────────────────
_ payload-part TypeId
    - payload TypeId
    - offset U32

` The part of a case's payload in a place, where it is a tuple.
match types.rows[payload]
    | .type-tuple(row)
        if offset < row.fields.count then types.child-type(row.fields, offset) else no-type
    ??
        no-type

────────────────────
_ do type-entered
    - owner SyntaxId
    - items [SyntaxId]

` What runs where a body is entered, once its entry statements have: what its first case is
` given where it is entered so (`enters-initial`), which a case's never is where one of its
` immediate transitions always passes (`always-passes`), its immediate transitions, each with
` its condition, or its subject matched by its pattern, and what it gives, then the stream of
` each of its groups (`type-group`).
. initial = if owner == 0 || !tree.always-passes(items) then tree.initial-case(items) else 0
if initial != 0 && tree.enters-initial(machining.items, owner)
    type-targets(initial)
for transition in tree.immediate-transitions(items)
    . trigger = tree.state-trigger(transition)
    . subject = tree.trigger-subject(trigger)
    if trigger == 0
        type-targets(transition)
        continue
    if subject != 0
        type-trigger-pattern(trigger, infer(subject))
    else
        . condition = tree.trigger-condition(trigger)
        note-truthiness(condition, condition, infer(condition))
    type-targets(transition)
for head in tree.group-heads(items)
    type-group(owner, head)

────────────────────
+ do type-trigger-pattern
    - trigger SyntaxId
    - subject TypeId

` A trigger's pattern matched against what it tests: an item of its stream, or the subject of
` an `if | p = s`.
. pattern = tree.trigger-pattern(trigger)
if pattern == 0 || subject == invalid-type || subject == no-type
    =
do match? tree.nodes[pattern]
    | .node-structure-match(row)
        check-pattern(row.pattern, subject)
        =
check-pattern(pattern, subject)

────────────────────
_ do type-group
    - owner SyntaxId
    - head SyntaxId

` A group of event transitions where its owner subscribes it, as the reference makes it: its
` stream is made a `Broadcastable`, recorded at its first transition's trigger, and the
` machine's `Subscriber` of its item is given to the broadcaster's `subscribe` and
` `unsubscribe`, whose errors are given to the global `unhandled-error` (`hands-off-raising`),
` each call kept with the group. What a call of the
` subscriber answers is kept for its type. A stream that is neither is the reference's error
` at the transition. One on an event of an object is typed so too (`type-event-group`), and one
` on a stream that is iterable and implements no `Broadcastable` itself, though it may convert
` to one, as `type-iterated-group` says, as the reference tries them in that order.
. trigger = tree.group-trigger(head)
. written = tree.group-stream(head)
if tree.trigger-kind(trigger) == StateTriggerKind.state-trigger-whenever
    . watched = watched-stream(trigger, written)
    if watched != no-type
        subscribe-group(owner, head, watched)
    =
. found = infer-found(written, Want().adding(.want-event))
. given = found.type
if found.event != U32.max
    . event = found-events[found.event]
    type-event-group(owner, head, trigger, written, event, given)
    =
if given == invalid-type || given == no-type
    =
if types.broadcastable-decl.module == 0
    decline(head)
    =
if interface-of(given, types.broadcastable-decl) == no-type && iterates-as-source(given)
    type-iterated-group(owner, head, trigger, written, given)
    =
. stream = supported(given, types.broadcastable-decl)
if stream == no-type
    frame.diagnose
        - head
        - .stated
        - program.store-atom("State trigger source is not broadcastable or iterable")
    =
conversions.convert(trigger, written, given, stream, .reason-argument)
facts.set-node-type(instance, trigger, stream)
subscribe-group(owner, head, stream)

────────────────────
_ do subscribe-group
    - owner SyntaxId
    - head SyntaxId
    - stream TypeId

. item = first-arg(stream)
. subscriber = types.well-known-type-of("core/stream", "Subscriber", item)
if item == no-type || subscriber == invalid-type
    decline(head)
    =
. subscribing = calls.protocol-call(stream, program.store-atom("subscribe"), head, subscriber, false, no-type, no-type, false)
if subscribing.answer == invalid-type
    decline(head)
    =
. subscribe = subscribing.fact
. unsubscribing = calls.protocol-call(stream, program.store-atom("unsubscribe"), head, subscriber, false, no-type, no-type, false)
if unsubscribing.answer == invalid-type
    decline(head)
    =
. unsubscribe = unsubscribing.fact
if !hands-off-raising(subscribe) || !hands-off-raising(unsubscribe)
    decline(head)
    =
. carried = carried-result(types, subscriber)
if carried != no-type
    types.complete(carried)
    facts.note-carried(function-row(types, subscriber), carried)
. enqueue = machine-enqueue(item, subscriber)
if enqueue == no-instance
    decline(head)
    =
. group = MachineGroup
    - head
    - owner
    - stream
    - item
    - subscriber
    - subscribe
    - unsubscribe
    - U32.max
    - false
    - false
    - enqueue
machining.groups-found += group

────────────────────
_ do watched-stream TypeId
    - trigger SyntaxId
    - written SyntaxId

if !tracks-reads(tree, written)
    . message = "A \"whenever\" trigger fires as what it reads with \"#\" changes, and this one reads nothing with \"#\", so it would never fire; write \"#\" before what it follows, as in \"whenever #feed\""
    frame.diagnose(trigger, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
    = no-type
if types.live-action-type == invalid-type
    decline(trigger)
    = no-type
. given = infer(written)
if given == invalid-type || given == no-type
    = no-type
. read = demand-lambda(given, scratch.no-types)
if read == no-instance
    decline(trigger)
    = no-type
. value = instances.signatures[read].returns
if value == invalid-type || value == no-type
    = no-type
. module = class-ref(types, types.live-action-type).module
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(value)
scratch.types.push(given)
. watch = calls.demand-runtime-call(module, no-type, program.store-atom("watch-changes"), mark, 1)
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
if watch == no-instance
    decline(trigger)
    = no-type
conversions.convert(trigger, written, given, instances.argument-type(watch, 0), .reason-argument)
do facts.record-call(instance, trigger, watch, .call-function, scratch.no-fills, false)
. stream = instances.signatures[watch].returns
facts.set-node-type(instance, trigger, stream)
= stream

────────────────────
_ do machine-enqueue InstanceId
    - item TypeId
    - subscriber TypeId

` The event runtime's `event-machine-enqueue` of an item, which the reference gives a group's
` activation, an item and its broadcaster, to run the activation once no event is being
` published and no other transition runs; or none.
. broadcaster = types.well-known-type-of("core/stream", "Broadcastable", item)
if broadcaster == invalid-type || types.event-endpoint-decl.module == 0
    = no-instance
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(item)
scratch.types.push(subscriber)
scratch.types.push(item)
scratch.types.push(broadcaster)
. name = program.store-atom("event-machine-enqueue")
. found = calls.demand-runtime-call(types.event-endpoint-decl.module, no-type, name, mark, 1)
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
= found

────────────────────
+ do iterates-as-source Bool
    - container TypeId

` Whether the reference finds the items of the stream of a group of a machine's event
` transitions by iterating it: a generator, or a value `supported` as an `Iterable`, an
` `Indexable` or a `Stream`.
if same-decl(class-ref(types, container), types.generator-decl)
    = true
for decl in [types.iterable-decl, types.indexable-decl, types.stream-decl]
    if supported(container, decl) != no-type
        = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do type-iterated-group
    - owner SyntaxId
    - head SyntaxId
    - trigger SyntaxId
    - written SyntaxId
    - given TypeId

` A group of event transitions on a stream that is only iterable, as the reference makes it
` where its owner subscribes it: the container is read at once, by its protocol planned at the
` trigger, which has the slots of a loop, and each item is given to the group's handler with
` the container. The reference's loop there does not poll.
. iterated = iteration-container(given, written)
. item = loop-item-type(iterated, trigger)
if item == invalid-type || item == no-type
    decline(head)
    =
note-container-iteration(trigger, iterated, false, trigger)
if is-indexed(iterated, false)
    facts.set-plan(instance, trigger, .plan-index-loop)
    if is-array-field(iterated, types.length-atom!)
        facts.set-constant(instance, trigger, ConstantFact(1, 0, null, false), .plan-index-loop)
    keep-loop(trigger, iterated, types.size-type, types.size-type)
keep-loop-item(trigger, item)
. subscriber = types.well-known-type-of("core/stream", "Subscriber", item)
if subscriber == invalid-type || facts.plan-of(instance, trigger) == .plan-none
    decline(head)
    =
machining.groups-found += MachineGroup
    - head
    - owner
    - iterated
    - item
    - subscriber
    - no-fact
    - no-fact
    - U32.max
    - false
    - true

────────────────────
_ do type-event-group
    - owner SyntaxId
    - head SyntaxId
    - trigger SyntaxId
    - written SyntaxId
    - event NamedEvent
    - stream TypeId

` A group on an event of an object, as the reference subscribes it: the endpoint the event
` runtime keeps for the object's event is the group's `Broadcastable`, and the machine keeps a
` port of the event runtime for the group, which queues each item that arrives on the event
` runtime's machine queue and runs the machine's subscriber with it. The port is made where
` the group is first subscribed, and attached to the endpoint and detached from it where its
` owner enters and exits. A group the event runtime runs from the table of a class instead
` (`lowers-group`) needs `event-register-lowered`, and its port is made where the machine
` starts and given what the table runs it with. One at the address of a keyed event takes the
` endpoint there, which the receiver claims, and is never run from the table, as the
` reference's `keyed-address-required` decides.
. keyed = event.address != 0
if (event.key != no-type && !keyed) || stream == invalid-type || stream == no-type
    decline(head)
    =
. endpoint = if keyed then event-call("event-keyed-endpoint", event.payload, no-type, 3) else event-call("event-endpoint", event.payload)
. item = event.payload
. subscriber = types.well-known-type-of("core/stream", "Subscriber", item)
. broadcastable = types.well-known-type-of("core/stream", "Broadcastable", item)
. port-type = types.well-known-type-of("core/event", "EventMachinePort", item)
if endpoint == no-instance || subscriber == invalid-type || unportable
    decline(head)
    =
.. unportable = broadcastable != stream || port-type == invalid-type
if keyed && !claim-endpoint(head, head, event.address, endpoint)
    =
conversions.convert
    - trigger
    - written
    - instances.signatures[endpoint].returns
    - stream
    - .reason-argument
facts.set-node-type(instance, trigger, stream)
. lowered = if keyed then false else lowers-group(owner, written, event)
if !lowered
    =
if lowered! && facts.event-register == no-instance
    demand-event-register()
if lowered! && facts.event-register == no-instance
    decline(head)
    =
. carried = carried-result(types, subscriber)
if carried != no-type
    types.complete(carried)
    facts.note-carried(function-row(types, subscriber), carried)
. held = types.optional-of(port-type)
. port = if lowered then port-call("event-machine-port", item, subscriber, stream) else no-instance
. post = if lowered then port-call("event-machine-post", item, port-type, item) else no-instance
. attach = if lowered then no-instance else port-call("event-machine-attach", item, held, subscriber, stream)
. detach = if lowered then no-instance else port-call("event-machine-detach", item, held)
. made = if lowered then port != no-instance && post != no-instance else attachable
    .. attachable = attach != no-instance && detach != no-instance
if !made
    decline(head)
    =
. used = facts.event-uses.length as U32
facts.event-uses += EventUse
    - instance
    - head
    - written
    - event.owner
    - event.name
    - .event-subscribe
    - endpoint
    - no-instance
    - no-instance
    - event.address
instances.mark-may-panic(instance)
. group = MachineGroup
    - head
    - owner
    - stream
    - item
    - subscriber
    - no-fact
    - no-fact
    - used
    - lowered
    - false
    - no-instance
    - port
    - post
    - attach
    - detach
machining.groups-found += group

────────────────────
_ do port-call InstanceId
    - name String
    - item TypeId
    - first TypeId
    - second TypeId = no-type
    - third TypeId = no-type

` A function of the event runtime that keeps the port of a machine's group on an event of an
` object, with the group's item as its type argument, given arguments of the types after it.
. mark = scratch.types.mark
scratch.types.push(item)
scratch.types.push(first)
if second != no-type
    scratch.types.push(second)
if third != no-type
    scratch.types.push(third)
. called = calls.demand-runtime-call
    - types.event-endpoint-decl.module
    - no-type
    - program.store-atom(name)
    - mark
    - 1
scratch.types.rewind(mark)
= called

────────────────────
_ do lowers-group Bool?
    - owner SyntaxId
    - written SyntaxId
    - event NamedEvent

` Whether the event runtime runs a group of a machine's event transitions from the table of the
` class whose object it is written for, as the reference plans it: a group at the root of a
` machine a property of the class holds, or of one written in the class's content, as
` `lowers-for` decides. A group of a case of the same machine on the event is planned first, as
` the reference compiles the cases a transition enters before the machine's root, and is no such
` group, which leaves the root's group to the sidecar path the reference then takes.
. stored = machining.store == .store-member || machining.store == .store-content
if !stored || owner != 0 || frame.self-type == no-type
    = false
. lowered = lowers-for(frame.self-type, module, written, event)
if lowered == null
    decline(written)
= lowered

────────────────────
+ do lowers-for Bool?
    - receiver TypeId
    - source ModuleId
    - written SyntaxId
    - event NamedEvent

` Whether the event runtime runs a group at the root of a machine, written in a module on a
` stream, from the table of a class: one on an event of the object itself, its name alone or
` read from `this`. Where a section of the class or of one above it hears the event too, or a
` constructor of one of them subscribes to it, the reference subscribes the group itself. Where
` a group of another of their machines is on it, the reference's choice turns on the order it
` compiles them in, and the group has no shape here (null).
. found = own-event(receiver, source, written)
if !found || found.owner != event.owner || found.name != event.name
    = false
. chain [TypeId]
. level TypeId? = receiver
while level
    chain += level
    level = types.base-of(level)
. groups = 0u32
. hearing = 0u32
for holder in chain
    . ref = class-ref(types, holder)
    for part in sheet-parts(ref)
        . part-module = program.modules[part.module]
        for member in part-module.member-pool[part-members(part)]
            do match? part-module.decls[member]
                | .decl-rule(rule)
                    . heard = section-event(receiver, part.module, rule.syntax)
                    if heard && heard.owner == event.owner && heard.name == event.name
                        = false
                | .decl-property(property)
                    . machine = if property.name && !property.is-lazy then machine-node else 0
                        .. machine-node = part-module.tree.declared-machine(property.value)
                    if machine != 0
                        . heard = event-groups
                            - part-module.tree
                            - part-module.tree.state-items
                                - part-module.tree.state-body(machine)
                            - event.name
                        groups += heard
                        hearing += if heard != 0 then 1 else 0
    . owner-module = program.modules[ref.module]
    do match? owner-module.decls[ref.decl]
        | .decl-class(class)
            for machine in owner-module.tree.content-machines(class.content)
                . heard = event-groups
                    - owner-module.tree
                    - owner-module.tree.state-items(owner-module.tree.state-body(machine))
                    - event.name
                groups += heard
                hearing += if heard != 0 then 1 else 0
for heard in constructor-events(receiver, chain)
    if heard.owner == event.owner && heard.name == event.name
        = false
if hearing != 1
    = null
= groups == 1

────────────────────
_ do event-groups U32
    - tree AST
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - name Atom

` How many groups of event transitions in a body, and in the bodies of its transitions, are on
` an event of the object itself of a name, written alone or read from `this`.
. count = 0u32
for head in tree.group-heads(items)
    . stream = tree.group-stream(head)
    do match? tree.nodes[stream]
        | .node-identifier(row)
            if row.name == name
                count += 1
        | .node-get-expression(get)
            if get.name == name
                do match? tree.nodes[get.object]
                    | .node-identifier(object)
                        if object.name.text == "this"
                            count += 1
for item in items
    if tree.is-transition(item)
        count += event-groups(tree, tree.state-items(tree.state-body(item)), name)
= count

────────────────────
_ do group-item TypeId
    - head SyntaxId

` The item the stream of a group gives, or no type where its group has no shape.
for group in machining.groups-found
    if group.head == head
        = group.item
= no-type

────────────────────
_ do type-handlers
    - owner SyntaxId
    - items [SyntaxId]

` The function each group of a body's event transitions runs for an item: `each` and `it` are
` the item, and each transition matches its pattern, tests its guard and gives its targets; a
` handler runs its loop (`type-state-handler`).
for head in tree.group-heads(items)
    . item = group-item(head)
    if item == no-type
        continue
    . each = bindings.declared-kind-at(frame.slots, head, .slot-each)
    . it = bindings.declared-kind-at(frame.slots, head, .slot-it)
    if each != no-slot
        frame.assign(each, item)
    if it != no-slot
        frame.assign(it, item)
    if tree.is-state-handler(head)
        type-state-handler(head, item)
        continue
    for transition in tree.group-transitions(items, head)
        . trigger = tree.state-trigger(transition)
        type-trigger-pattern(trigger, item)
        . guard = tree.trigger-guard(trigger)
        if guard != 0
            note-truthiness(guard, guard, infer(guard))
        type-targets(transition)

────────────────────
_ do type-state-handler
    - head SyntaxId
    - item TypeId

` A handler's loop where an item of its stream arrives, as the reference runs it: its pattern
` binds the item, its `when` is tested, and then its body runs, as the handler `handling` names.
do match? tree.nodes[head]
    | .node-for-block(row)
        do match? tree.nodes[row.loop]
            | .node-loop-syntax(loop)
                if loop.pattern != 0
                    check-pattern(loop.pattern, item)
                do match? tree.nodes[loop.clause]
                    | .node-clause(clause)
                        note-truthiness(clause.expr, clause.expr, infer(clause.expr))
                . outer = handling
                handling = head
                do check-statement(row.body)
                handling = outer

────────────────────
_ do type-targets
    - transition SyntaxId

` What a transition gives the case it enters, typed where it fires. The source of a case's
` payload settles what the case holds where nothing did before (`fixed-payload`), and each
` name the case keeps takes what it reads there, which every transition that enters the case
` where the name is in reach must agree on, as the reference unifies them. A transition into a
` case that names what it holds gives one value for each name (`gives-names`).
for target in tree.children[tree.state-targets(transition)]
    do infer(target)
if !gives-names(transition)
    =
machining.typed += transition
. position = tree.case-position(machining.cases, tree.state-name(transition)!)
if position == null
    =
settle-payload(position, transition)
for read in bindings.machine-reads
    if read.module != module || read.site != transition
        continue
    . place = machining.kept[position].find(read.name)
    if place == null
        continue
    if read.slot == no-slot
        continue
    . read-type = frame.slot-type(read.slot)
    if read-type == no-type || read-type == invalid-type
        decline(transition)
        continue
    . known = machining.kept-types[position][place]
    if known == no-type
        machining.kept-types[position][place] = read-type
    else if known != read-type
        . joined = relations.unify(known, read-type, module)
        if relation-legal(joined)
            machining.kept-types[position][place] = joined.unified
        else
            frame.diagnose
                - transition
                - .stated
                - program.store-atom
                    - "Unable to unify activation capture type for '${read.name.text}'"

────────────────────
_ do gives-names Bool
    - transition SyntaxId

` Whether a transition gives a case that names what it holds, written with no trigger of its
` own, a value for each name, which is reported where it does not.
. name = tree.state-name(transition)
. held = if name then tree.find-case(machining.items, name) else 0
if held == 0 || held == transition || tree.state-trigger(held) != 0
    = true
. names = tree.state-targets(held).count
. given = tree.state-targets(transition).count
if names == 0 || given == names
    = true
. holds = if names == 1 then "one value" else "$names values"
. gives = if given == 0 then "none" else "$given"
. message = "Case \"${name!.text}\" holds $holds, and this transition gives $gives; give it $holds"
frame.diagnose(transition, .stated, program.store-atom(message))
= false

────────────────────
_ do settle-payload
    - position U32
    - transition SyntaxId

` What a case holds, once the transition that is the source of its payload is typed, from what
` it gives (`settle-given`).
if machining.payloads[position] != no-type
    =
. source = tree.payload-source(machining.items, tree.state-name(machining.cases[position])!)
if !source || source.node != transition
    =
. given [TypeId]
for target in tree.children[tree.state-targets(transition)]
    given += facts.node-type(instance, target)
settle-given(position, given)

────────────────────
_ do settle-given
    - position U32
    - given [TypeId]

` What a case holds, from what the source of its payload gives: each part joined with what each
` other transition that gives the case values gives in its place, where that is known
` (`join-others`), and the one part, or a tuple of them.
join-others(position, given)
if given.length == 1
    machining.payloads[position] = given[0]
    =
. mark = scratch.types.mark
. names-mark = scratch.names.mark
for offset in 0 .. < given.length
    scratch.names.push(types.index-atom(offset as U32))
    scratch.types.push(given[offset])
machining.payloads[position] = types.intern-tuple(mark, names-mark)

────────────────────
_ do join-others
    - position U32
    - given [TypeId]

` Joins what the source of a case's payload gives with what each other source that gives values
` gives in its place, as the reference joins them: what one typed already gives, or what one
` gives typed on trial apart from where it fires (`source-given`). One whose values are not
` known so, that gives another number of them, or whose values do not join, is left out, and
` its values are converted to what the case holds where it fires.
for type in given
    if type == no-type || type == invalid-type
        =
. name = tree.state-name(machining.cases[position])!
. best = tree.payload-source(machining.items, name)
for source in tree.payload-sources(machining.items, name)
    if (best && source.node == best.node) || gives-nothing(source)
        continue
    . other = source-given(source.node)
    if other.length != given.length
        continue
    . joined [TypeId]
    for offset in 0 .. < given.length
        . part = join-payload(given[offset], other[offset])
        if part == no-type || part == invalid-type
            break
        joined += part
    if joined.length == given.length
        for offset in 0 .. < given.length
            given[offset] = joined[offset]

────────────────────
_ do source-given [TypeId]
    - node SyntaxId

` What a transition that gives a case values gives: the types of its targets where it is typed,
` or else typed on trial where it is written, with the names the activations around it see
` (`trial-transition`). None where any is unknown.
. found [TypeId]
if machining.typed.find(node) != null
    for target in tree.children[tree.state-targets(node)]
        found += facts.node-type(instance, target)
else
    . chain [SyntaxId]
    . items = source-place(machining.items, node, chain)
    if items.length == 0
        = found
    . slots [SlotId]
    . known [TypeId]
    for part in chain
        activation-names(part, slots, known)
    . wanted [SlotId]
    . captured [TypeId]
    trial-transition(node, items, slots, known, wanted, captured, found)
for type in found
    if type == no-type || type == invalid-type
        found.clear()
        break
= found

────────────────────
_ do source-place [SyntaxId]
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - node SyntaxId
    - chain [SyntaxId]

` The items of the body of a machine a node is written among, with the cases and
` continuations whose bodies hold them added to `chain`, outermost first; none where it is not
` written there.
for item in items
    if item == node
        = items
    if tree.is-transition(item)
        chain += item
        . inner = source-place(tree.state-items(tree.state-body(item)), node, chain)
        if inner.length != 0
            = inner
        chain.pop()
. none [SyntaxId]
= none

────────────────────
_ do join-payload TypeId
    - held TypeId
    - given TypeId

` The type two values a case is given in one place join to, as the reference joins inferred
` types: an optional of the other where one is `null`, or what they unify to, or invalid.
if held == given
    = held
if held == types.null-type || given == types.null-type
    . other = if held == types.null-type then given else held
    = types.optional-of(types.optional-inner(other))
. relation = relations.unify(held, given, module)
= if relation-legal(relation) then relation.unified else invalid-type

────────────────────
_ do machine-union TypeId
    - id SyntaxId
    - row MachineSlots

` The union a machine's value is, private to it: a case for each case it names, in the order it
` names them, holding what that case holds. It is named, as the reference names it, for the
` local, the global or the property that names the machine, and numbered among the machines of
` the module, and told apart by that number, which an edit that moves the machine's lines keeps.
. name = "StateMachine"
. property = machine-property(id)
if row.bound != no-slot
    name = "${state-type-name(bindings.slots[row.bound].name)}State"
if machining.store == .store-nested && machining.named
    name = "${state-type-name(machining.named)}State"
do match? program.modules[module].decls[property]
    | .decl-property(found)
        if property != 0 && found.name
            name = "${state-type-name(found.name)}State"
. mark = scratch.types.mark
. names-mark = scratch.names.mark
for position in 0 .. < machining.cases.length
    scratch.names.push(tree.state-name(machining.cases[position])!)
    scratch.types.push(machining.payloads[position])
. number = machine-number(id)
= types.intern-named-union(program.store-atom("$name$number"), mark, names-mark, module, number)

────────────────────
_ do state-type-name String
    - name Atom

` A name as the reference writes it in a type's: each part between hyphens with its first
` letter made upper case, joined.
. text = ""
for part in name.text.split("-")
    if part.length != 0
        text = "$text${part[0 .. < 1].uppercased}${part[1 ...]}"
= text

────────────────────
_ do machine-number U32
    - id SyntaxId

` The place of a machine among those its module writes, counted from one.
. count = 0u32
for row in bindings.machines
    if row.module == module && row.syntax <= id
        count += 1
= count

────────────────────
_ do type-machine-slots
    - row MachineSlots
    - union TypeId

` What a machine keeps, in its own function's environment: its value, and for each case its
` flag, its generation, what it holds, where it holds anything, and each name it keeps, whose
` first value is typed where it is a named tuple or struct, which a case keeps where nothing
` entering it captures the name; for each group the subscriber the machine gave its broadcaster
` and the broadcaster, while it is subscribed, or for a group on an event the port the machine
` keeps for it once it is made. A case whose activation owns the tasks spawned for it keeps the
` `TaskOwner` it makes as it is entered (`demand-task-owner`). Flags declared beside the local a
` machine is kept in are of the function the machine is written in.
assign-kept(row, row.syntax, "(value)", union)
for position in 0 .. < machining.cases.length
    . node = machining.cases[position]
    assign-kept(row, node, "(active)", types.bool-type)
    assign-kept(row, node, "(generation)", types.type-row(.uint32))
    if bindings.machine-slot(row, node, program.store-atom("(tasks)")) != no-slot
        demand-task-owner()
        assign-kept(row, node, "(tasks)", types.optional-of(types.task-owner-type))
    if machining.payloads[position] != types.void-type
        assign-kept(row, node, "(payload)", machining.payloads[position])
    . kept = machining.kept[position]
    for place in 0 .. < kept.length
        assign-kept(row, node, "(kept ${kept[place].text})", machining.kept-types[position][place])
        demand-first-values(machining.kept-types[position][place])
for group in machining.groups-found
    . port = if group.port != no-instance then instances.signatures[group.port].returns else no-type
    . attached = if group.attach != no-instance then attach-type else port
        .. attach-type = instances.signatures[group.attach].returns
    . subscriber = if attached != no-type then attached else group.subscriber
    assign-kept(row, group.head, "(subscriber)", types.optional-of(subscriber))
    assign-kept(row, group.head, "(source)", types.optional-of(group.stream))

────────────────────
_ do assign-kept
    - row MachineSlots
    - node SyntaxId
    - name String
    - type TypeId

. slot = bindings.machine-slot(row, node, program.store-atom(name))
if slot == no-slot
    =
. own = bindings.machine-slot(row, row.syntax, program.store-atom("(value)"))
if own != no-slot && bindings.slots[slot].scope != bindings.slots[own].scope && frame.outer
    frame.outer.assign(slot, type)
else
    frame.assign(slot, type)

────────────────────
_ do type-projections
    - id SyntaxId
    - store MachineStore

` Each projection of a machine written as a statement, a local of the function it is written in
` named after a case: the case's flag, or what it holds where it is active.
if store != .store-none || !frame.outer
    =
for position in 0 .. < machining.cases.length
    . name = tree.state-name(machining.cases[position])!
    . slot = bindings.declared-at(frame.outer!.slots, id, name)
    . payload = machining.payloads[position]
    if slot != no-slot
        frame.outer!.assign
            - slot
            - if payload == types.void-type then types.bool-type else types.optional-of(payload)

────────────────────
_ do convert-targets

` What each typed transition gives, converted to the part of what its case holds in its place,
` or to all of it, at each value.
for transition in machining.typed
    . position = tree.case-position(machining.cases, tree.state-name(transition)!)
    if position == null
        continue
    . payload = machining.payloads[position]
    . targets = tree.state-targets(transition)
    . offset = 0u32
    for target in tree.children[targets]
        . part = if targets.count == 1 then payload else payload-part(payload, offset)
        . given = facts.node-type(instance, target)
        if part != no-type && given != no-type && given != invalid-type
            conversions.convert(target, target, given, part, .reason-argument)
        offset += 1

────────────────────
_ do trial-transition
    - transition SyntaxId
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - slots [SlotId]
    - given [TypeId]
    - wanted [SlotId]
    - found [TypeId]
    - targets [TypeId]

` What a transition of a machine, written among a body's items, sees and gives, typed on trial
` apart from where it fires (`trial-checker`) with the names its activation sees holding the
` types given, as the reference infers what a case holds and the names it keeps: the type of
` each slot wanted once its trigger's pattern has matched (`foresee-transition`), added to
` `found`, and of each of its targets, added to `targets`. None of either where the part that
` gives them reports anything.
. checker = trial-checker(transition)
for offset in 0 .. < slots.length
    if given[offset] != no-type && given[offset] != invalid-type
        checker.frame.assign(slots[offset], given[offset])
. reported = facts.diagnostics.length
checker.foresee-transition(transition, items, wanted, found, targets)
facts.diagnostics.truncate(reported)
checker.close()
checker.retire()
